_Rosetta.register_constructor(PSplineRegression, _PSplineRegression, 2039, false)
"""
    PSplineRegression(x::Any, y::Any, n_basis::Integer) -> PSplineRegression
    PSplineRegression(x::Any, y::Any, n_basis::Integer, lambda::Float64, degree::Integer=3, penalty_order::Integer=2) -> PSplineRegression
    PSplineRegression(x::Any, y::Any, knots::Any) -> PSplineRegression
    PSplineRegression(x::Any, y::Any, knots::Any, lambda::Float64, degree::Integer=3, penalty_order::Integer=2) -> PSplineRegression

`n_basis` cubic B-splines with equally spaced knots over the range of `x`; λ chosen
by GCV.
Searches log10(lambda) on [-8,8] in steps of 0.5, then uses golden-section refinement
around the best grid point. Singular candidates score infinity. This bounded refinement
does not guarantee a global continuous minimum. Penalty order is two.

**Example**

```cpp
const dm::Vector<> x=dm::seql(0,1,30);
const dm::PSR fit(x,dm::sin(6*x),10);
std::print(\"{}\\n\",fit.lambda()>0); // true
```

**References**

- G. H. Golub, M. Heath and G. Wahba (1979). Generalized cross-validation as a
  method for choosing a good ridge parameter. https://doi.org/10.1080/00401706.1979.10489751

# Throws

- `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid data or basis size.
- `std::runtime_error`: If all candidate systems fail numerically.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `gcv()`, `smoothing_path()`.

`n_basis` B-splines of the given `degree` with equally spaced knots over the range of
`x`, penalized with smoothing parameter `lambda` on differences of order `penalty_order`.

**Example**

See the class example for a degree-one, order-two fit.

# Throws

- `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid data/options or non-finite extended knots.
- `std::runtime_error`: If the penalized system is singular or non-finite.
- `std::overflow_error`: If difference weights or the penalty overflow.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `PSplineRegression`, `fda::fit_pspline()`.

Cubic basis on the given knot locations; boundary knots are the smallest/largest of
`knots` and `x`. The difference penalty assumes roughly even spacing. λ chosen by GCV.
Uses the same bounded GCV search as the basis-count constructor.

**Example**

```cpp
const dm::Vector<> x=dm::seql(0,1,30);
const dm::PSR fit(x,dm::sin(6*x),dm::seql(0,1,8));
std::print(\"{}\\n\",fit.basis_size()); // 10
```

# Throws

- `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid data/knots or zero-width combined domain.
- `std::runtime_error`: If every candidate system fails numerically.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `PSplineRegression`, `gcv()`, `knots()`.

Basis on the given knot locations with a fixed smoothing parameter `lambda`.
Outer spacings are continued past the domain, without repeated boundary knots.
The penalty acts on coefficient index and does not correct for unequal knot spacing.

**Example**

```cpp
const dm::PSR fit({0,1,2},{0,1,0},dm::Vector<>{0,1,2},1.0,1,2);
std::print(\"{:.6f}\\n\",fit.predict({1})[0]); // 0.428571
```

# Throws

- `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid data, options, knots or zero-width combined domain.
- `std::runtime_error`: If the system is singular or non-finite.
- `std::overflow_error`: If difference weights or the penalty overflow.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `PSplineRegression`, `fda::pspline_difference_matrix()`.

# Arguments
- `x::Any`: Nonempty finite coordinates spanning a positive-width interval.
- `y::Any`: Finite responses matching x.
- `n_basis::Integer`: Basis count K, at least four.
- `n_basis::Integer`: Basis count at least degree+1 and greater than penalty_order.
- `lambda::Float64`: Finite nonnegative multiplier of summed squared coefficient differences.
- `degree::Integer`: Polynomial degree, default three.
- `penalty_order::Integer`: Positive difference order, default two.
- `x::Any`: Nonempty finite coordinates.
- `y::Any`: Finite matching responses.
- `knots::Any`: Nonempty finite breakpoints, sorted/deduplicated and enlarged to contain x.
- `lambda::Float64`: Finite nonnegative smoothing multiplier.
- `penalty_order::Integer`: Positive difference order smaller than the resulting basis, default two.
"""
PSplineRegression(args...) = _Rosetta.construct(PSplineRegression, args)

