- `std::invalid_argument`: If the coordinates are empty or differ in length, or `type` is not one of the three codes.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `RPlot(std::vector<double>`, `std::vector<double>)`, `points()`, `lines()`.

# Arguments
- `x::Vector{Float64}`: Horizontal coordinates, one per point.
- `y::Vector{Float64}`: Vertical coordinates, paired with `x` by position.
- `type::String`: `\"p\"` (default), `\"l\"`, or `\"b\"`; case-sensitive.
- `label::String`: Legend text; empty (the default) keeps the plot out of the automatic legend. With `\"b\"` only the line carries it.
- `color::RGB`: Color of the points and line (default blue `{37, 99, 235}`).

# Returns
`RPlot`: A new plot holding the series.

(Static method of `RPlot`.)
