- `std::invalid_argument`: If `values` is empty, has a negative entry, or sums to 0, or `names` is nonempty with a different length.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `polygon()`, `text()`.

# Arguments
- `values::Vector{Float64}`: Wedge sizes; nonnegative, with a positive sum.
- `names::Vector{String}`: Wedge labels; empty (the default) draws none.
- `colors::Vector{RGB}`: Wedge colors, recycled; empty (the default) uses the built-in palette.

# Returns
`RPlot`: A new plot holding one Polygon series per wedge plus one Text series per name.

(Static method of `RPlot`.)
