- `std::invalid_argument`: Empty/nonfinite samples or invalid alternative.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `HypothesisTestResult`.

# Arguments
- `x::Vector{Float64}`: Nonempty finite first sample.
- `y::Vector{Float64}`: Nonempty finite independent second sample.
- `alternative::Symbol`: TwoSided (default); Greater tests F_x above F_y, Less below, so Greater corresponds to stochastically smaller x.

# Returns
`HypothesisTestResult`: statistic=D or D+/D-, parameter1=n_x, parameter2=n_y and approximate p_value; no CI.
"""
ks_test_two_sample(x, y) = _Rosetta.call(193, (x, y))
ks_test_two_sample(x, y, alternative) = _Rosetta.call(193, (x, y, alternative))

"""
    shapiro_francia_test(x::Vector{Float64}) -> HypothesisTestResult

Shapiro-Francia composite normality test, like R nortest::sf.test().

Squared correlation of sorted observations with Blom normal scores, using Royston (1993) log-
normal p-value approximation. Tests some normal distribution; a large p-value does not prove
normality. Rounding/ties affect calibration. O(n log n) work/O(n) storage; input unchanged, no
omission/shared state.

**Example**

```cpp
