- `std::invalid_argument`: Invalid sample sizes/values, alternative/confidence, unrepresentable mean difference or zero/nonfinite combined standard error.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `HypothesisTestResult`.

# Arguments
- `x::Vector{Float64}`: At least two finite observations in the first group.
- `y::Vector{Float64}`: At least two finite independent observations in the second group.
- `equal_variance::Bool`: False (default) uses Welch; true uses pooled variance.
- `alternative::Symbol`: TwoSided (default), Less or Greater for mean(x)-mean(y).
- `conf_level::Float64`: Finite confidence level in (0,1), default .95.

# Returns
`HypothesisTestResult`: statistic=t, parameter1=df, estimate1/2=group means, p_value and confidence bounds for their difference. One-sided bounds can be infinite.
"""
t_test_two_sample(x, y) = _Rosetta.call(202, (x, y))
t_test_two_sample(x, y, equal_variance) = _Rosetta.call(202, (x, y, equal_variance))
t_test_two_sample(x, y, equal_variance, alternative) = _Rosetta.call(202, (x, y, equal_variance, alternative))
t_test_two_sample(x, y, equal_variance, alternative, conf_level) = _Rosetta.call(202, (x, y, equal_variance, alternative, conf_level))

"""
    t_test_paired(x::Vector{Float64}, y::Vector{Float64}, alternative::Symbol=:TwoSided, conf_level::Float64=0.95) -> HypothesisTestResult

Paired Student t-test on aligned differences, like R t.test(paired=TRUE).

Runs the one-sample test on x[i]-y[i]. Differences, rather than the two marginal samples, need
independent normal sampling for the exact t reference. Row order defines pairing; no values
are omitted. O(n) work/storage; inputs unchanged, no shared mutable state.

**Example**

