- `std::filesystem::filesystem_error`: For an empty path, a conflicting file, insufficient permissions or other operating-system filesystem errors.

C++ exceptions are raised as `NativeError`.

See also: `std::filesystem::create_directories()`.

# Arguments
- `path::String`: Directory to create, including any missing parents; must not be empty.

# Returns
`Bool`: True if the target directory was created, false if it already existed.
"""
mkdir(path) = _Rosetta.call(208, (path,))

